<p>The stellar initial mass function of <span class="citation" data-cites="Kroupa2001">Kroupa (2001)</span> is a broken power law:</p>
<p><span id="eq-kroupa"><img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?%0A%5Cfrac%7BdN%7D%7BdM_%5Cstar%7D%20%5Cpropto%20M_%5Cstar%5E%7B-%5Calpha%7D,%20%5Cqquad%0A%5Calpha%20=%20%5Cbegin%7Bcases%7D%0A0.3%20&amp;%20M_%5Cstar%20%3C%200.08%5C,M_%5Codot%20%5C%5C%0A1.3%20&amp;%200.08%5C,M_%5Codot%20%5Cle%20M_%5Cstar%20%3C%200.5%5C,M_%5Codot%20%5C%5C%0A2.3%20&amp;%20M_%5Cstar%20%5Cge%200.5%5C,M_%5Codot%0A%5Cend%7Bcases%7D%0A%5Ctag%7B1%7D"></span></p>
<p>Figure&nbsp;1 plots Equation&nbsp;1 per logarithmic mass interval.</p>
